<!--
  XSD Render Target — README
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.target.xsd.README
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:xsd="org.blockml.bml.target.xsd">

  <name>README</name>
  <type>xsd:README</type>
  <baseType>core:ReadMe</baseType>
  <is>Reading entry for the XSD render target</is>

  <documentation>
    @blockml/xsd-target implements RenderTarget name xsd (Phase C after BlockDoc).
    Generates XSD artifacts from BML / Definition meta-model — not a Stage-1 parser
    dependency (B8 / D5). V1 emits bml.xsd for all block roots: identity and
    container particles from D1 defaults and authored bml:xml / xmlRendering.
    Also emits types.xsd and service.xsd (org.blockml.bml.type.* /
    org.blockml.bml.service.* vocabulary) and writes catalog.xml at the project
    root mapping namespace URIs to ./schemas/*.xsd for IDE offline resolution.
    Unknown child elements of block are invalid (no xs:any wildcard). Attributes
    stay lax via xs:anyAttribute so xmlns / xsi:schemaLocation remain legal.
    Target namespace http://blockml.org/bml.
    Compile: blockml compile xsd (library/corpus/auto). Default outDir schemas/.
    Domain schemas can be disabled via targetOptions.xsd.emitDomainSchemas: false.
    Validating authored BML against generated schemas is out of this package's
    generate path and must stay disableable (--no-xsd / xsdValidation).
  </documentation>

</block>
